  "body": "The quick gate on a branch that contains `upstream/main` 409c0b5ab has one red test.\n\n**Test:** `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test feature_edge_g1_join`, test `no_pickable_edge_is_a_tangent_piece_of_a_longer_one_in_any_step_fixture`.\n\n**Output:**\n\n```\nbar_cross_holes.step: 3701 pickable edges, 39259 chains, 116 split pieces\n```\n\nAll other STEP fixtures read `0 split pieces`.\n\n**Cause (not confirmed by a bisect):** the test reads each STEP file in `testdata/models/`. The file `testdata/models/bar_cross_holes.step` is new on `main` (it came with the merge of PR #2565). The test was green on `upstream/main` 370d38df6, which did not have that file. The branch where this was seen (`issue/1444-slot-undercut`, PR for #1444) does not change STEP import, feature edges or this test.\n\n**Not done:** the test was not run on a clean checkout of `main`. The evidence is the merged branch only.\n\n**Fix sketch:** make the feature-edge join law hold for `bar_cross_holes.step` (see #2215 for the law), or keep the new fixture out of this test with a stated reason.\n\n**Done means:** `feature_edge_g1_join` is green on `main` with the fixture in the tree.\n",
